# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  LIVE — ONE BOX AT A TIME, WATCHING ~150 STOCK UNDERLYINGS AT ATM±1, LONG BOX ONLY
#  Broker: Zerodha (Kite).  Exactly one exchange lot per leg.
#
#  This profile exists because the shipped one-box templates watch a SINGLE index. Watching a wide
#  STOCK universe is a different configuration problem, and getting it wrong is silent: the engine
#  reports a healthy feed and simply never finds anything, or finds everything on one name.
#
#  WHAT MAKES THIS FILE DIFFERENT FROM deploy/FINAL-one-box-live.env.template
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. BOX_ALLOW_STOCK_UNDERLYINGS=true. The default is FALSE, and false DELETES every stock
#      option chain during the universe pass. Watching 150 stocks without this yields 0 stocks.
#   2. BOX_MAX_UNDERLYINGS=150 instead of 1, with the token budget raised to match.
#   3. BOX_LIVE_ALLOWED_UNDERLYINGS is EMPTY, not "NIFTY". That allowlist is an ENTRY filter: left
#      at NIFTY it refuses entry on every stock, however good the opportunity.
#   4. The entry economics are LOT-RELATIVE (§15). This is the substantive fix — see below.
#   5. The quantity caps are sized for stock lots, not for an index lot of 65.
#
#  WHY THE ECONOMICS HAD TO CHANGE TO WATCH A WIDE UNIVERSE AT ALL
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  A box's edge is `grossEdgePerUnit × lotSize`, so it SCALES with the lot. Flat rupee gates do
#  not. F&O lots run from ~35 to 40,000+, so a single flat ₹1,200 gate + ₹150 buffer + ₹250/₹250
#  slippage is not one policy applied to 150 names — measured against the real code it is a
#  1,143x different per-unit requirement:
#
#      lot     35  ->  needs ₹52.857 per unit   (a ~50% dislocation: unreachable, ever)
#      lot     75  ->  needs ₹24.667 per unit
#      lot  1,000  ->  needs ₹ 1.850 per unit
#      lot 10,000  ->  needs ₹ 0.185 per unit
#      lot 40,000  ->  needs ₹ 0.046 per unit   (inside the bid-ask noise: hit constantly)
#
#  That is why opportunities were rare AND always in the same few names: the gate excluded most of
#  the universe by arithmetic and waved through the largest lots. The per-unit rates below resolve
#  as `max(flat, rate × lotSize)` per candidate, so one setting means one hurdle everywhere.
#
#  READ BEFORE THE FIRST SESSION
#  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   * Every «EDIT» line must be filled in. Secrets are intentionally blank.
#   * Run this in BOX_EXECUTION_MODE=paper_legging FIRST for at least one full session and read
#     GET /api/box/status → scanner rejection counters. Tune §15 against what you actually see
#     before switching §8 to live. The numbers in §15 are a defensible STARTING POINT, not a
#     promise about how often a real box will clear them.
#   * Before RUN, read GET /api/box/universe. `summary.watched` is how many names actually have a
#     window; `eligible_not_watched` > 0 means a CAP is choosing for you, and `blocked_by_caps`
#     with `inadmissible_reason` names anything that can never trade at these quantity limits.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ═══ §1. PROCESS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
PORT=3001
NODE_ENV=production
APP_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata
SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=20000

# «EDIT» Public origin of the SPA. CSRF_ALLOWED_ORIGIN must match it exactly (scheme + host).
FRONTEND_URL=https://CHANGEME.example
CSRF_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://CHANGEME.example


# ═══ §2. IDENTITY / LOCK NAMESPACE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# «EDIT» Stable per-deployment identity. Two processes sharing this ID share execution locks —
# which is the point in a failover pair and a disaster between unrelated environments.
CALSPREAD_DEPLOYMENT_ID=CHANGEME-prod-aws-mumbai
BOX_DEPLOYMENT_REGION=ap-south-1
CALSPREAD_INSTANCE_ID=


# ═══ §3. POSTGRESQL — THE OPERATIONAL AUTHORITY ══════════════════════════════════════════════
# «EDIT»
DATABASE_URL=
PG_POOL_MAX=10
PG_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
PG_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS=2000
PG_APPLICATION_NAME=gts
PG_MIGRATE_ON_BOOT=true


# ═══ §4. ACCESS GATE ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# «EDIT»
SITE_ACCESS_SECRET=
SITE_SESSION_TTL_HOURS=24
SESSION_COOKIE_NAME=gts_session


# ═══ §5. BROKER TOKEN STORAGE ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# «EDIT» 32-byte key, base64. Losing it invalidates every stored broker token.
BROKER_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
